WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.610 --> 00:00:05.350
The Los Angeles Rams may have taken home the
trophy for winning the 2022 Super Bowl, but

00:00:05.350 --> 00:00:10.400
Marvel fans were big winners too, getting
two new trailers for a pair of highly anticipated

00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:12.799
Marvel Cinematic Universe projects.

00:00:12.799 --> 00:00:17.530
One was a 30-second TV spot for the upcoming
Disney+ show "Moon Knight," giving viewers

00:00:17.530 --> 00:00:21.290
a much closer look at the Oscar Isaac-led
superhero project.

00:00:21.290 --> 00:00:22.870
But that was just the appetizer.

00:00:22.870 --> 00:00:27.490
Marvel Studios served up an entire meal with
a new full-length "Doctor Strange in the Multiverse

00:00:27.490 --> 00:00:28.880
of Madness" trailer.

00:00:28.880 --> 00:00:33.550
The "Doctor Strange" sequel is directed by
Sam Raimi, whose work on the original "Spider-Man"

00:00:33.550 --> 00:00:38.520
trilogy is largely why those three films are
still well regarded among superhero movie

00:00:38.520 --> 00:00:39.520
fans.

00:00:39.520 --> 00:00:43.150
Benedict Cumberbatch is set to return as the
titular Doctor Strange, and he is joined by

00:00:43.150 --> 00:00:48.060
Elizabeth Olsen as Wanda Maximoff, a character
who hasn't been seen in the MCU since the

00:00:48.060 --> 00:00:49.300
end of "WandaVision."

00:00:49.300 --> 00:00:54.230
The finale of that Disney+ series not only
cemented Wanda's MCU transformation into the

00:00:54.230 --> 00:00:59.020
Scarlet Witch, but also shows her starting
to truly explore the limits of her magical

00:00:59.020 --> 00:01:00.020
powers.

00:01:00.020 --> 00:01:03.190
Since the "Multiverse of Madness" trailer
was released, Marvel fans have dissected it

00:01:03.190 --> 00:01:07.271
frame-by-frame for clues and Easter eggs,
and some believe they've found one that may

00:01:07.271 --> 00:01:10.120
shed further light on Wanda's true intentions.

00:01:10.120 --> 00:01:13.920
When viewers finally catch up with her again,
it looks like the Scarlet Witch may still

00:01:13.920 --> 00:01:17.030
be crafting her own intricate, believable
illusions.

00:01:17.030 --> 00:01:21.409
In the "Wandavision" finale, Wanda flees to
a remote location where she begins to study

00:01:21.409 --> 00:01:26.180
a powerful arcane book known as the Darkhold
in hopes of learning how to control and further

00:01:26.180 --> 00:01:28.630
hone her previously unpredictable powers.

00:01:28.630 --> 00:01:33.100
Now, fans are getting a much clearer understanding
of the person Wanda has become by the time

00:01:33.100 --> 00:01:34.600
"Multiverse of Madness" picks up.

00:01:34.600 --> 00:01:38.680
There are two brief moments, in particular,
in the film's second trailer that fans have

00:01:38.680 --> 00:01:39.680
picked up on.

00:01:39.680 --> 00:01:43.659
The first features Wanda and Doctor Strange
chatting as they stroll through a lush, green

00:01:43.659 --> 00:01:44.659
orchard.

00:01:44.659 --> 00:01:47.479
Strange, having just dealt with the events
of "Spider-Man: No Way Home," asks,

00:01:47.479 --> 00:01:48.960
"What do you know about the multiverse?"

00:01:48.960 --> 00:01:53.240
A little later, it seems the two characters
are in the same location, but the scenery

00:01:53.240 --> 00:01:54.310
has changed.

00:01:54.310 --> 00:01:57.909
Not only does Wanda seem to have swapped out
her regular clothes for her Scarlet Witch

00:01:57.909 --> 00:02:02.790
costume, but she is also shown facing Strange
in what appears to be an ominous, overwhelmingly

00:02:02.790 --> 00:02:04.010
red environment.

00:02:04.010 --> 00:02:07.450
The trailer may want viewers to believe these
two shots come from different scenes in the

00:02:07.450 --> 00:02:10.810
movie, but MCU fans seem to think they're
one in the same.

00:02:10.810 --> 00:02:15.849
As sleuthing fan LongjumpingTrainer38 pointed
out on Reddit, the framing of these two scenes

00:02:15.849 --> 00:02:20.470
is nearly identical, with Wanda seen over
Stephen's shoulder and vice versa.

00:02:20.470 --> 00:02:24.580
Also, Stephen Strange appears to be wearing
the same outfit and scarf during both his

00:02:24.580 --> 00:02:28.849
normal, pleasant conversation with Wanda and
his slightly more antagonistic interaction

00:02:28.849 --> 00:02:31.489
with her in that strange, crimson environment.

00:02:31.489 --> 00:02:35.220
In one shot, the trees in Wanda's orchard
are also shown to be in bloom.

00:02:35.220 --> 00:02:36.620
In another, they're barren.

00:02:36.620 --> 00:02:40.760
If Marvel fans are correct, the most likely
explanation for these two seemingly different

00:02:40.760 --> 00:02:45.319
environments is that the lush, green setting
we initially see Wanda and Strange walking

00:02:45.319 --> 00:02:49.770
through is an elaborate illusion Wanda has
whipped up to mask her surroundings.

00:02:49.770 --> 00:02:55.640
In response to LongjumpingTrainer38's observation
and theory about the two moments, PeterParker72

00:02:55.640 --> 00:02:56.640
remarked,

00:02:56.640 --> 00:02:57.640
"Very nice catch.

00:02:57.640 --> 00:02:59.099
Can't wait to see how this plays out."

00:02:59.099 --> 00:03:03.760
At this point in the MCU's timeline, creating
an illusion like the one fans are theorizing

00:03:03.760 --> 00:03:06.260
about would be child's play for Wanda.

00:03:06.260 --> 00:03:09.970
After all, she successfully hexed an entire
town in "WandaVision."

00:03:09.970 --> 00:03:12.900
"I made mistakes, and people were hurt."

00:03:12.900 --> 00:03:17.060
Understandably, the possibilities presented
by this theory have also led fans to begin

00:03:17.060 --> 00:03:22.440
speculating about the greater implications
of Wanda's reality-warping powers in "Multiverse

00:03:22.440 --> 00:03:23.440
of Madness."

00:03:23.440 --> 00:03:26.410
Redditor Rich_Acanthisitta_70, for one, wrote,

00:03:26.410 --> 00:03:28.300
"I have a feeling she'll be the villain.

00:03:28.300 --> 00:03:29.300
At first.

00:03:29.300 --> 00:03:32.739
I think it's a feint for a bigger bad in the
second act though."

00:03:32.739 --> 00:03:34.530
Redditor Bruhmangoddman commented,

00:03:34.530 --> 00:03:38.910
"The MCU deserves its fair share of fallen
heroes and raging psychopaths.

00:03:38.910 --> 00:03:41.440
If Wanda manages to be both, I'm all in."

00:03:41.440 --> 00:03:46.000
Now, all fans have to do is wait to find out
all the implications of Wanda and Strange's

00:03:46.000 --> 00:03:53.150
mysterious conversation in "Multiverse of
Madness," which releases on May 6, 2022.

